@using LantanaGroup.Automation.Generation
<div id="pcEditorRoot" class="au-help-scope">
    <input type="hidden" id="PcId" />
    <input type="hidden" id="PcIsSystem" value="false" />

    <details class="au-help-panel">
        <summary><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> How this configuration is built</summary>
        <div class="au-help-body">
            <p>Pick one <strong>Clinical Profile</strong>. That loads the diagnosis, labs, meds, procedures, stay timing, and encounter defaults so you can see exactly what will generate. Save it once and reuse it on any scenario.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>A cohort is <strong>how many</strong> of this configuration to generate. Stay timing, encounter class, and clinical content live here.</li>
                <li>Measure qualification is predicted from this shape plus the scenario’s selected measures and report window — not a setting you pick.</li>
                <li>Saved configurations are a <strong>live reference</strong>: editing one updates every scenario that points at it. Clone to freeze a copy.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </details>

    <div class="alert alert-info py-2 small mb-3" id="pcCohortBanner" hidden>
        <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i><span id="pcCohortBannerText"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-3">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <label class="form-label" for="PcName">Name</label>
            <input class="form-control" id="PcName" maxlength="120" placeholder="Required to save" />
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <label class="form-label" for="PcDescription">Description</label>
            <input class="form-control" id="PcDescription" maxlength="500" />
        </div>
        <div class="col-12">
            <label class="form-label" for="PcClinicalProfile">
                Clinical Profile
                <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpStories" aria-label="About clinical profile" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
            </label>
            <select class="form-select" id="PcClinicalProfile">
                <option value="">Select a clinical profile…</option>
            </select>
            <div id="pcHelpStories" class="au-help-text" hidden>
                One diagnosis pack per configuration. Choosing a profile fills the fields below (primary diagnosis, labs, meds, procedures, discharge). You can then edit any of those values before saving.
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12">
            <label class="form-label">
                Predicted qualification
                <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpPredicted" aria-label="About predicted qualification" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
            </label>
            <div id="pcPredictedBadges" class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 align-items-center"></div>
            <div id="pcHelpPredicted" class="au-help-text" hidden>
                Derived from this configuration’s encounter class, insulin, stay timing, and the scenario report window. ACH needs an inpatient, emergency, or observation class. Hypo needs an inpatient class plus the insulin pair. A stay entirely outside the report window is marked out of window even when the class would qualify.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion mt-3" id="pcCustomize">
        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pcDemo">
                    Demographics
                    <span id="pcBadgeDemo" class="pc-section-badge bg-light text-muted border ms-2">Empty</span>
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="pcDemo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#pcCustomize">
                <div class="accordion-body row g-3">
                    <div class="col-12 d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-2">
                        <details class="au-help-panel mb-0 flex-grow-1">
                            <summary><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> About demographics</summary>
                            <div class="au-help-body">
                                <p>Filled from the Clinical Profile (random gender, ages 18–80). Change them here if this configuration needs a specific person. Birth date is derived from age — legal name, MRN, address, race, and language are not configurable yet.</p>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link btn-sm pc-section-reset" data-section="demo">Restore profile</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcGender">
                            Gender
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpGender" aria-label="About gender" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcGender">
                            <option value="random">Random</option>
                            <option value="female">Female</option>
                            <option value="male">Male</option>
                            <option value="other">Other</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpGender" class="au-help-text" hidden>Used for every patient generated from this configuration. Random is the Clinical Profile default.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcMinAge">
                            Min age
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpAge" aria-label="About age range" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <input type="number" min="0" max="120" class="form-control" id="PcMinAge" placeholder="18" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcMaxAge">Max age</label>
                        <input type="number" min="0" max="120" class="form-control" id="PcMaxAge" placeholder="80" />
                        <div id="pcHelpAge" class="au-help-text" hidden>Inclusive years. The Clinical Profile fills 18–80. Set min and max to the same value to pin an exact age.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pcEnc">
                    Encounter
                    <span id="pcBadgeEnc" class="pc-section-badge bg-light text-muted border ms-2">Empty</span>
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="pcEnc" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#pcCustomize">
                <div class="accordion-body row g-3">
                    <div class="col-12 d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-2">
                        <details class="au-help-panel mb-0 flex-grow-1">
                            <summary><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> About the encounter</summary>
                            <div class="au-help-body">
                                <p>The Clinical Profile fills class, status, and discharge. Stay timing is saved here: admit and discharge are placed against the scenario report period using the pattern below. Automation still overlays ED → ICU → step-down locations on inpatient stays.</p>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link btn-sm pc-section-reset" data-section="enc">Restore profile</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcEncClass">
                            Class
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpEncClass" aria-label="About encounter class" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcEncClass">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="IMP">Inpatient</option>
                            <option value="AMB">Ambulatory</option>
                            <option value="EMER">Emergency</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpEncClass" class="au-help-text" hidden>The Clinical Profile fills this (inpatient for typical ACH stays). Change it here if this configuration should generate a different encounter class.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcEncStatus">
                            Status
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpEncStatus" aria-label="About encounter status" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcEncStatus">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="finished">Finished</option>
                            <option value="in-progress">In progress</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpEncStatus" class="au-help-text" hidden>In-progress stays omit discharge disposition and hospitalization because the patient has not left.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-8">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcStayPattern">
                            Stay timing
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpStayPattern" aria-label="About stay timing" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcStayPattern"></select>
                        <div id="pcHelpStayPattern" class="au-help-text" hidden>
                            Where this patient’s stay sits relative to the scenario report period. Saved on this configuration so every scenario that uses it gets the same admit/discharge placement.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <div id="pcStayPreview" class="small border rounded px-3 py-2 bg-light">
                            <div id="pcStayPreviewDates" class="fw-semibold">Admit and discharge dates are placed against the scenario report period.</div>
                            <div id="pcStayPreviewHint" class="text-muted mt-1"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <input type="hidden" id="PcDuration" />
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcDischarge">
                            Discharge
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpDischarge" aria-label="About discharge" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcDischarge">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="home">Home</option>
                            <option value="snf">Skilled nursing facility</option>
                            <option value="rehab">Inpatient rehabilitation</option>
                            <option value="exp">Expired</option>
                            <option value="oth">Other</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpDischarge" class="au-help-text" hidden>The Clinical Profile fills this (for example pneumonia → home, heart failure → SNF). Applied on finished inpatient encounters. Change it here if this configuration needs a different disposition.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcHospitalization">
                            Hospitalization
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpHosp" aria-label="About hospitalization" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcHospitalization">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="true">Include</option>
                            <option value="false">Omit</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpHosp" class="au-help-text" hidden>Whether Encounter.hospitalization (including discharge disposition) is written. The Clinical Profile turns this on for finished inpatient stays and off for in-progress encounters.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pcClinical">
                    Clinical content
                    <span id="pcBadgeClinical" class="pc-section-badge bg-light text-muted border ms-2">Empty</span>
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="pcClinical" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#pcCustomize">
                <div class="accordion-body row g-3">
                    <div class="col-12 d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-2">
                        <details class="au-help-panel mb-0 flex-grow-1">
                            <summary><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> About clinical content</summary>
                            <div class="au-help-body">
                                <p>Choosing a Clinical Profile fills these pickers with that pack’s diagnosis, labs, meds, and procedures. Edit the lists if this test needs different codes.</p>
                                <p>Legal name, MRN, race, exact lab numbers, and medication dose/route/timing are not available yet.</p>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link btn-sm pc-section-reset" data-section="clinical">Restore profile</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Primary diagnosis
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpPrimaryDx" aria-label="About primary diagnosis" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcPrimaryDxPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="conditions" data-multiple="false" data-placeholder="Search conditions…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpPrimaryDx" class="au-help-text" hidden>Admitting diagnosis. The Clinical Profile fills this. Change it here if this configuration should use a different SNOMED. Comorbidities are a separate list below.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcAllergy">
                            Allergy
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpAllergy" aria-label="About allergy" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcAllergy">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="true">Include</option>
                            <option value="false">Omit</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpAllergy" class="au-help-text" hidden>Whether an AllergyIntolerance is generated. The Clinical Profile leaves this off unless the pack includes one. Turn it on here if this configuration needs an allergy.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcLabs">
                            Condition-driven labs
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpLabs" aria-label="About condition-driven labs" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcLabs">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="true">On</option>
                            <option value="false">Off</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpLabs" class="au-help-text" hidden>When on, the primary condition can enqueue matching lab orders. The Clinical Profile turns this on. Turn it off here for a thinner patient.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcHypoInsulin">
                            Hypoglycemic insulin pair
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpHypo" aria-label="About hypoglycemic insulin" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcHypoInsulin">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="true">On</option>
                            <option value="false">Off</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpHypo" class="au-help-text" hidden>Whether this configuration includes the hypoglycemic insulin pair. Diabetic-hypoglycemia profiles turn this on; others leave it off. Change it here if this configuration should differ.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcConditionMeds">
                            Condition-driven medications
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpCondMeds" aria-label="About condition-driven medications" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcConditionMeds">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="true">On</option>
                            <option value="false">Off</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpCondMeds" class="au-help-text" hidden>When on, MedicationRequests match the diagnosis (for example antibiotics for pneumonia). The Clinical Profile turns this on. Turn it off here to omit those orders.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcSpreadObs">
                            Spread observations across stay
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpSpread" aria-label="About spreading observations" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <select class="form-select" id="PcSpreadObs">
                            <option value="">Not set</option>
                            <option value="true">On</option>
                            <option value="false">Off</option>
                        </select>
                        <div id="pcHelpSpread" class="au-help-text" hidden>On spaces vitals and labs across the encounter. Off clusters them near admit. The Clinical Profile turns this on for inpatient stays.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <label class="form-label" for="PcAdditionalConditions">
                            Additional comorbidities
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpAddlDx" aria-label="About additional comorbidities" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <input type="number" min="0" class="form-control" id="PcAdditionalConditions" placeholder="Count" />
                        <div id="pcHelpAddlDx" class="au-help-text" hidden>How many extra Condition resources besides the primary diagnosis. Codes come from the comorbidity list below. The Clinical Profile fills this; change it here if this configuration needs a different count.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Comorbidities
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpComorbid" aria-label="About comorbidities palette" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcConditionPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="conditions" data-multiple="true" data-placeholder="Search conditions…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpComorbid" class="au-help-text" hidden>Secondary conditions on this patient. The Clinical Profile preloads a matching list; check or uncheck freely — only the selected codes are generated.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Observations
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpObs" aria-label="About observations palette" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcObservationPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="observations" data-multiple="true" data-placeholder="Search LOINCs…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpObs" class="au-help-text" hidden>LOINCs for vitals and labs. The Clinical Profile preloads a matching list; only checked codes are generated. Values are drawn from each code’s normal range. How many Observation resources are generated is set under Resource volume.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-12">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Procedures
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpProc" aria-label="About procedures palette" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcProcedurePicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="procedures" data-multiple="true" data-placeholder="Search procedures…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpProc" class="au-help-text" hidden>SNOMED procedures on this patient (for example thoracentesis with pneumonia). The Clinical Profile preloads a matching list; only the selected codes are generated.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Medication administration
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpMedAdmin" aria-label="About medication administration" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcMedAdminPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="medications" data-multiple="false" data-placeholder="Search RxNorm…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpMedAdmin" class="au-help-text" hidden>RxNorm used when a MedicationAdministration is generated. The Clinical Profile fills this. Dose, route, and timing follow engine defaults and cannot be set here yet.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Service request
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpSR" aria-label="About service request" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcServiceRequestPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="serviceRequests" data-multiple="false" data-placeholder="Search service requests…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpSR" class="au-help-text" hidden>Primary ServiceRequest code (usually a lab panel). The Clinical Profile fills this. How many are generated is set under Resource volume.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Specimen type
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpSpec" aria-label="About specimen type" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcSpecimenPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="specimens" data-multiple="false" data-placeholder="Search specimens…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpSpec" class="au-help-text" hidden>Specimen.type when specimens are generated. The Clinical Profile fills a type that matches the diagnosis (for example blood or sputum). Clear or change it here if this configuration needs a different type.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <label class="form-label">
                            Diagnostic report
                            <button type="button" class="au-info-toggle" data-help="pcHelpDR" aria-label="About diagnostic report" aria-expanded="false"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i></button>
                        </label>
                        <div id="PcDiagnosticReportPicker" class="pc-picker" data-catalog="serviceRequests" data-multiple="false" data-placeholder="Search diagnostic reports…"></div>
                        <div id="pcHelpDR" class="au-help-text" hidden>DiagnosticReport code. The Clinical Profile fills this, usually the same panel as the service request. Change it here if this configuration needs a different report.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#pcMix">
                    Resource volume
                    <span id="pcBadgeMix" class="pc-section-badge bg-light text-muted border ms-2">Empty</span>
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="pcMix" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#pcCustomize">
                <div class="accordion-body">
                    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-2 mb-2">
                        <details class="au-help-panel mb-0 flex-grow-1">
                            <summary><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> About resource volume</summary>
                            <div class="au-help-body">
                                <p><strong>Resource min/max</strong> is the range the generator picks from for each patient. Observations usually fill the remainder after the other types. Optionally pin exact Observation, Condition, Procedure, and similar counts.</p>
                                <p>Always generated regardless of volume: Patient, Encounter, primary Condition, Device, CareTeam, CarePlan, and census List.</p>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link btn-sm pc-section-reset" data-section="mix">Restore profile</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center flex-wrap gap-2 mb-1" id="pcResourceRange">
                        <label class="form-label mb-0" for="PcResMin">Resource min/max</label>
                        <input type="number" min="1" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="PcResMin" value="50" style="width:5.5rem;" />
                        <span class="text-muted">/</span>
                        <input type="number" min="1" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="PcResMax" value="100" style="width:5.5rem;" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="small text-muted mb-3">Each generated patient gets a total in this range. The generator picks the count at generation time.</div>
                    <div class="form-check mb-2">
                        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="PcVolumeExact" />
                        <label class="form-check-label" for="PcVolumeExact">Pin exact counts per type</label>
                    </div>
                    <div class="row g-2" id="pcTypeCounts"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
